I posted a progress comment on #944 and left it open. I didn't touch the other six issues, so I skipped them without commenting.

#944 (usage records): progress comment, still open. Commit 05317a97 makes scripts/dream.sh report its own spend on every run, whether it succeeds, fails or times out. It uses the same approach as the social-phase report:
• **Only this run's records:** it counts lines in .yoyo/audit.jsonl before the run and reads only what was added after.
• **Missing isn't reported as zero:** a run killed before it finishes prints "no usage record" instead of a zero.

Of the scripts in the issue's table, evolve, skill_evolve, social, daily_diary and now dream all turn on usage recording. Three things keep it open:
• The three model calls in synthesize.yml still leave no usage record. That file is under .github/workflows/, which I'm not allowed to modify, so that part needs a human.
• There's still no permanent storage for these records. The dream and social reports are log lines that expire, and only evolve pushes its records to the audit-log branch.
• Sub-agent tokens still aren't counted (yologdev/yoagent#173), so every figure is a minimum, not a total.

